# Exceptions and Errors

## Types

| Class | File | When thrown |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `BlingApiException` | `src/Exceptions/BlingApiException.php` | Bling returns a structured `error` object |
| `BlingInternalException` | `src/Exceptions/BlingInternalException.php` | Transport or library failure, or an error body that is not `ErrorResponse` |
| `BlingParseResponsePayloadException` | `src/Exceptions/BlingParseResponsePayloadException.php` | A union member rejects a payload during `from` |

## API error shape

`Entities\Shared\DTO\Error` is the only error model:

- `ErrorResponse` holds `Error $error`.
- `Error` holds `type`, `message`, `description`, and `ErrorField[] $fields`.
- `ErrorField` holds `code`, `msg`, `element`, `namespace`, and `ErrorFieldCollection[] $collection`.

`BlingApiException` sets `Exception::$message` from `error.description` and the code from the HTTP status. `getResponse(): ErrorResponse` returns the parsed body. `getHttpStatus(): int` returns the status.

`BlingInternalException` carries `?Headers $responseHeaders`, `?Body $responseBody`, the message, the code, and the previous throwable, in that order.

## Handling flow

`ResponseOptions::__construct` performs the translation described in `architecture/repository-layer.mdc`. Entities return `fromResponse(...)` and do not catch these exceptions.

Callers catch `BlingApiException` for a Bling error payload and `BlingInternalException` for a failed call or an unreadable payload.

`BaseResponseRootObject::throwForInconsistentResponseOptions` throws `BlingInternalException` when a success body is missing or unexpectedly present. Message: `Resposta inconsistente da API: {method} {endpoint}`.

## Union parsing

A schema `from` override throws `BlingParseResponsePayloadException` when the payload is a different variant. `BaseResponseObject::from` catches that exception while trying a union and continues with the next type (`ContasPagarOcorrenciaUnicaDTO`). Do not throw `BlingParseResponsePayloadException` for HTTP failures.

## Entity documentation

Every public entity method that calls `$this->repository` documents:

```
@throws BlingApiException|BlingInternalException
```

Follow the block in `src/Entities/Contatos/Contatos.php`.

## Extension rules

- Keep these three exception classes. Extend `Error`, `ErrorField`, or `ErrorFieldCollection` when Bling adds an error field.
- Do not read `error` inside an entity method.
- Do not build a second error DTO under an entity `Schema/` folder.
